  "id": "overcontrolled",
  "term": "overcontrolled",
  "definition": "Overcontrolled refers to a personality style marked by unusually high self-control, often described as constricted and associated with traits like introversion and restraint. In eating-disorder research, this style has most often been linked with anorexia nervosa and restricting forms of eating disorders.",
